lesson: 229
title: The school week
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A school week has 5 school days, Monday to Friday.
explain: A sandwich is made from 2 slices of bread with the filling in between.
explain: A sandwich every school day for 3 children: 3 × 2 = 6 slices a day, 6 × 5 = 30 slices a week; for 2 weeks, 30 × 2 = 60 slices.
vars: a=name c=2..4 w=2..4
answer: c * 2 * 5 * w
exercise: Every school day, {c} children each take a sandwich for lunch. How many slices of bread are used in {w} school weeks?
exercise: {a}'s dad makes a sandwich for each of his {c} children every school day. How many slices of bread does he use in {w} school weeks?
exercise: The {c} children in {a}'s family each eat one sandwich at school every school day. How many slices of bread do they eat in {w} school weeks?
exercise: A packed lunch has one sandwich. {c} children get a packed lunch every school day for {w} weeks of term. How many slices of bread are needed?
exercise: Grandma makes {c} sandwiches each school day for her grandchildren. How many slices of bread does she need for {w} school weeks?
exercise: {c} kids, sandwich each every school day, {w} weeks. how many slices i need to buy
exercise: mum does {c+1}, no {c} sandwiches each school day, how many slices for {w} weeks of school
exercise: packed lunch for {c} of us, {w} wks of school, slices?? and we leave the crusts lol
exercise: {a} reckons {c} sandwiches a day for {w} school weeks is {c*7*w} slices. right? how many
exercise: sambo each for {c} kids every school day, {w} weeks. slices of bread?
exercise: How many slices of bread make one sandwich for each of {c} children on every school day for {w} school weeks?
test: Over {w} weeks of school, how many slices of bread go into the sandwiches if {c} children have one sandwich each per school day?
test: The school kitchen makes one sandwich a day for each of {c} children, on school days only. How much bread, in slices, does it use in {w} school weeks?
test: {c} children, one sandwich each, every day they're at school, for {w} weeks. how many slices
test: {a} has a sandwich and an apple every school day, and so does everyone in {a.his} group of {c} friends, {a} included. How many slices of bread does the group use in {w} school weeks?
test: slices for {w} weeks of sandwiches for {c} kids on school days? weekends we have soup
test: On each of the school days, {c} pupils bring a sandwich; on Saturdays they play football. How many slices of bread are in their sandwiches over {w} school weeks?
exam: Determine the aggregate number of slices of bread required to furnish each of {c.words} pupils with one sandwich on every school day for a period of {w.words} school weeks.
exam: It is given that {c} children are each provided with a sandwich on every day of school attendance. Ascertain the number of slices of bread consumed over {w} school weeks.
exam: A household prepares one sandwich per child per school day for {c} children. State the number of slices of bread so required in respect of {w} school weeks.
exam: Compute the total quantity of bread, in slices, expended upon sandwiches for {c} pupils, one each per school day, throughout {w} school weeks.
exercise: Money's a bit tight since Dad was let go, so Mum makes packed lunches instead of paying for school dinners: a sandwich every school day for each of her {c} children. How many slices of bread does she use in {w} school weeks?
exercise: we're "cash-strapped", aka skint, so it's sarnies for school. {c} kids, one sarnie each every school day, {w} weeks. how many slices, quick
test: {a} was economical with the truth when {a.he} said Mum never packs sandwiches: she makes one for each of her {c} children every school day. How many slices of bread does she use in {w} school weeks?
